body:
### Tested versions

- Reproducible in: 4.7.2.stable.mono, 4.8.dev7.mono
- Does not seem reproducible with GDScript, C#-only

### System information

Godot v4.7.2.stable.mono - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9186) - AMD Ryzen 5 5600 6-Core Processor (12 threads) - 31.91 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)

### Issue description

<details><summary>Base issue: categories not recognized as class categories</summary>
<p>

On project load or reload, C# script are not recognized as such in the inspector. Their categories are treated as custom categories, like if they were written with the ExportCategoryAttribute.

Building the project again **does not solve the issue**. For the scripts to be properly acknowledged, you need to make a change in your codebase first and then build the project. This is reproducible on Tool and non-Tool scripts.

Although it is hacky, parsing the tooltips of the EditorInspectorCategory node is currently the simplest way to know if we're dealing with a class category or a custom category (please do let me know if I'm wrong 🙌). Reflection could be used but would be a bit more cumbersome to set up. In the broken situation, the class category nodes tooltips are their label, instead of "class|*".

<img width="1806" height="1658" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a324f3ae-0270-428e-aadd-2e88d85f1fed" />

</p>
</details> 

<details><summary>EDIT - Inheritance case: class category is fully skipped</summary>
<p>

In case with inheritance, where the inherited class features a CustomCategory on its first field, this class' category will be fully ignored. 

```c#
public partial class MyClassA : Node3D
{
    [ExportCategory("Class A Custom Category On First Field")]
    [Export] int myClassAInt;

    [ExportCategory("Class A Custom Category")]
    [Export] Aabb myClassAAabb;
}
``` 

```c#
public partial class MyClassB : MyClassA
{
    [Export] Vector3 myClassBVector3;

    [ExportCategory("Class B Custom Category")]
    [Export] bool myClassBBool;
}
``` 

<img width="1500" height="860" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/55483c75-10a8-44ce-9d59-7c256b5477a1" />

This InspectorPlugin will never print "Parsing MyClassA" in the faulty case, it's not considered.
```c#
public partial class InspectorPlugin : EditorInspectorPlugin
{
    public override bool _CanHandle(GodotObject @object)
    {
        return true;
    }
    public override void _ParseCategory(GodotObject @object, string category)
    {
        base._ParseCategory(@object, category);
        GD.Print($"Parsing {category}");
    }
}
```
</p>
</details> 


### Steps to reproduce

* Open and build the MRP: the categories are correct on the nodes in the MRP scene
* Select "Reload Current Project" or close and reopen: the categories are incorrect
* Build project: the categories are still incorrect
* Make any change (line break/comment/uncomment) in the code and build: the categories are correct

### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)

MRP:
[unrecognized_classes.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/33282352/unrecognized_classes.zip)

MRP with a header category/inheritance issue:
[unrecognized_classes_with_plugin.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/33302006/unrecognized_classes_with_plugin.zip)
